    },
    "body": "pointer_gate_supervision=1.0 on the pointer arm configuration, interface read first (it is a scalar loss weight, not a file). The gate rose and stayed up: mean gate 0.2644 without supervision to 0.4638 early, settling at 0.4164 at step 12,207, with dev_gate_bce 0.6489. The panel regressed: I do appears on six of fifteen items and The sky returns for the yes/no sky item where the ungated arm complied. I am NOT claiming the Ana. item this time - the previous round verification showed that panel position is a turn-1 echo, and the emitted-value test must go through the probe on values in no store family. So the gate was necessary but not sufficient: raising it 60 percent did not produce the answer and cost compliance, meaning weight 1.0 is too strong for the mixture and too weak to lift the gate into the 0.6-1.0 copying band; the pre-registered prediction is partly falsified. Next is a weight sweep at 0.1 and 0.3 read with the probe seven rows. The value-driven copying result from the ungated arm is unaffected. References #820",
